{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 3, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "i think \"the social network\" is a very interesting movie. it tells the story of how facebook was created and the problems that the founder, mark zuckerberg, faced. the movie shows how mark, who was a student at harvard university, made a website called \"facemash\" which compared the photos of two students and asked people to vote on who was more attractive. this website became very popular, but it also got mark into trouble.\n\nafter that, mark was approached by some students who wanted him to make a website for harvard students only, where they could share information and photos. mark agreed, but he also worked on his own project, which later became facebook. the movie shows how facebook quickly became popular not just at harvard, but at other universities as well.\n\nthe movie also talks about the legal issues that mark faced. the students who initially asked mark to make the website for harvard claimed that mark stole their idea and sued him. mark also had problems with his friend eduardo saverin, who helped him financially at the beginning but later felt betrayed when mark changed the shares of the company.\n\ni think the actors in the movie did a good job. jesse eisenberg played mark zuckerberg very well, showing his intelligence and his social awkwardness. andrew garfield played eduardo saverin, and his performance showed the sadness and anger of being pushed away by his friend. the movie also had a good soundtrack, which made the scenes more exciting.\n\noverall, i think \"the social network\" is a good movie because it shows how a simple idea can become something very big, but it also shows the negative side of success, like losing friends and facing lawsuits. i would recommend this movie to anyone who is interested in technology and the story behind facebook.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -0.05090492591261864}, {"toke